1|0@relationships^1438956608#ctus90l:Adelaidey$:Remember: It won't be a baby for long in the scheme of things. In a few years, it's going to think that you're the coolest, wisest, most capable person in the entire world. That's going to be really really great when you're in your early twenties and feeling adrift.
14|0@relationships^1438925078#ctuiafh:Durbee$:My husband is an only, and funnily enough, no more than an hour ago I was telling him how much I wished he'd had the chance to experience welcoming a sibling into the family, the kind of wonder you have holding something so tiny and precious for the very first time and what showing them the ropes on life felt like. How you could love and be annoyed by and adore and be adored by this other little person who now was part of your crew - how you were no longer alone in your little lifeboat. Your world is about to change, and not all of it is going to be sunshine and gummy bears, but there will be times when your heart will be melted by a little fleshy, grubby, hardly coordinated kid that somehow knows that you will always keep them safe. He didn't get to have that, but you do. So breathe, trust your folks with your worries and your hopes, and do this as a team - because that's what you guys are, and will still be, when player 4 enters the game.
