104|0@relationships^1438914266#ctud08w:OIP$:hey man, fears are fears. 1. you're gonna get a kid sibling, that's great. kids are hilarious. you get to be an older brother (hell with that age gap you're gonna be more like a cool uncle). 2. yes, things will probably change. some things will and some things won't. none of the changes involve you being 'replaced'. 3. parents who are good at loving one kid are going to be pretty good at loving all of their kids. 4. overall, as general advice, it sounds like you might do well to try and feel things out on your own two feet. to get a solid sense of self under you so you're not as shaken up by changes. this is naturally going to be happening at 16 anyway. everything's going to be good. it's exciting. enjoy it.
