1|0@relationships^1439213869#ctxx8ca:xdaybreakerx$:Hey man, it's okay. I have a sibling 4 years younger than me, and one who is 12 years younger. It's scary. Kids are weird. Especially when you haven't had any siblings in your life to deal with before such a point in time. Babies suck. They smell, scream, poop, cry, vomit and are just generally a mess. But I can honestly say, the most rewarding experience of my life has been seeing my youngest sibling grow up to the person they are today. Be a big brother, be a father-figure. It's tough. It's rewarding. It's just another stage in life (and if you're anything like me - it's the most successful method of promoting safe sex because babies are not fun to live with). On a more different note, go get therapy. It sounds like you need it. If you're in school, there's probably services that are free for you. Talk to your mum about what you're feeling, and talk to a professional. 
